No such luck, I'm afraid.  There is no way to tell by inspection alone
whether the key predicates of an argument are vaguely or precisely defined.
Formally, "dilcu" (x1 is the quotient of x2 and x3 with remainder x4) is
indistinguishable from "derxi" (x1 is a heap of material x2 at location x3),
although one can be precisely defined and the other not.

